Although both statements return the same numbers, 2result.sql handles edge‑cases more gracefully (e.g. when max = min it still assigns bucket 1 and it clamps any overshoot back to bucket 10) and avoids repetitive scalar sub‑queries by using a single CROSS JOIN with the pre‑computed min/max values. This makes it both slightly safer and more efficient, so it is the better choice.

```plaintext
2result.sql
```